# Ruling 2025-07-25: "If the copied permanent is a token, the tokens that are created copy the original characteristics of that
# token." Bot1 casts Devastating Onslaught (X=1) on its Llanowar Elves, making token A, and then a second Onslaught (X=1) on
# token A itself, making token B, a copy of a copy of a token: both are 1/1 green Elf Druid creatures with haste and the
# Elves' mana ability, exactly as the Elves is. Six mana pay for both (Black Lotus's {R}{R}{R}, Mox Ruby, Mox Jet, Mox
# Emerald; the Elves would add more). All tokens are sacrificed at the beginning of the end step: the original Elves remains.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Devastating Onslaught
Devastating Onslaught
Llanowar Elves
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Devastating Onslaught.Cast(Llanowar Elves; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#2.Token = true
Bot1.Hand.Devastating Onslaught.Cast(Llanowar Elves#2; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#1.Token = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#3.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#3.Subtypes = Druid; Elf
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#3.Colors = Green
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#3.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#3.Keywords = Haste
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Graveyard = Devastating Onslaught; Devastating Onslaught; Black Lotus
